From f5dbe2dbba83d98f9d0d9139d33559ed57a8af6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: softisp: af: wait for the exposure, restart on exposure
 changes, black-level corrected measure, flat curve = failure

Hardware results on the Galaxy S10+ rear wide camera: a continuous-mode
scan started while AE was still settling (exposure 2.7 ms -> 66 ms); the
first, underexposed measurement (0.0233, 40x the rest) won and the lens
went to 0. In a dark scene the curve was flat (0.00229..0.00239) and the
lens was still sent to the "peak".

- A scan waits until exposure x gain and the level have stayed within
  10 % for two statistics in a row (at most 25 statistics, ~3.3 s), and
  restarts (up to 3 times) when either moves by more than 20 % against
  the scan start.
- The measure is taken on the level above black in 8 bit units (the
  statistics now say how to scale their luminance samples, afDiv), so
  the black level no longer distorts the normalisation.
- A scan whose highest/lowest measure ratio is below minPeakRatio (1.15)
  fails (AfState Failed) and the lens goes back to where it was before
  the scan, or to failPosition from the tuning file.
---
